.docname {Chat}
.include {docs}

.glossary
    | Word | Meaning | Example |
    |---|---|---|
    | Conversation | One person's thread of questions and answers | "Library heating" |
    | Exchange | One question and its answer | "Is room 2 hot?" and the reply |
    | History window | The last messages sent along with a new question | Last 10 |
    | SSE | Server-Sent Events: the answer arrives word by word on one open response | Text appearing as it is written |
    | Frame | One piece of that stream | A word, or "done" |

Realises the [Knowledge & Assistance](../domain-model/domain-assistance.qd) domain, with `agent`. Rust, MongoDB. Code-level page: [Chat Service](../services/chat.qd).

`chat` remembers conversations. `agent` answers one question at a time and remembers nothing. Together they make a conversation.

---

## Who talks to it

.mermaid
    flowchart LR
        C["client"] -- "conversations, questions" --> Ch["chat"]
        Ch -- "question, history, same claims" --> A["agent"]
        Ch --> DB[("MongoDB")]

---

## Inside

.mermaid
    flowchart LR
        H["HTTP, and the stream"] --> UC["Use cases: create, list, open, rename, delete, ask"]
        UC --> D["Rules: limits, history, titles"]
        UC --> P["Ports: store, assistant"]
        P -.-> M["MongoDB"]
        P -.-> AG["agent, streamed"]

Two things outside, so two ports. A test fails the build if a layer imports the wrong way.

---

## Asking a question

.mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        participant C as client
        participant Ch as chat
        participant A as agent
        C->>Ch: question
        Note over Ch: owner? limits? room left?
        Ch->>A: question and last 10 messages
        A-->>Ch: words, as written
        Ch-->>C: words, as written
        A-->>Ch: done, final answer
        Note over Ch: save the exchange now
        Ch-->>C: done, with the saved message

| Rule | Why |
|---|---|
| Only the last 10 messages go along | A long conversation does not grow the cost of each question |
| Stream, do not wait | The first words show in milliseconds, not seconds |
| Save only at the end | A broken answer leaves no half message behind |
| Forward the same claims | `agent` acts with the person's own rights, no more |

**Errors depend on timing.** Before the first word: a normal error status, like `404`. After: the status line is already sent as `200`, so the error comes as a last frame.

---

## Limits

| What | Limit |
|---|---|
| Messages per conversation | 100 |
| Characters per message | 8000 |
| Characters per title | 120 |

Checked before anything is saved.

- A new conversation is called "New chat". The first question becomes its title after the first answer.
- Every action checks owner and conversation together. Someone else's conversation answers "not found", so its existence does not leak.
- The edge must not hold the stream back. Caddy needs `flush_interval -1` on `/chat`.
